slettes automatisk etter tidens utløp. Nedenfor kan du kan se en komplett liste over cookies. Slik avviser eller sletter du cookies Du kan til enhver tid avvis cookies på datamaskinen, nettbrettet eller telefonen din ved å endre innstillingene i nettleseren din. Hvor du finner innstillingene, avhenger av hvilken nettleser du bruker. Hvis du endrer innstillingene må du være oppmerksom på at enkelte funksjoner og tjenester ikke kan brukes, da de forutsetter at nettsiden kan huske de valgene du gjør. Du kan velge bort cookies fra Google Analytics her . Det er mulig å velge bort enkelte annonsenettverk som deler opplysninger på tvers av forskjellige nettverk her . Sletting av cookies Cookies som du har akseptert tidligere, kan senere slettes. Benytter du en PC med en nyere nettleser, kan du slette cookies ved å bruke hurtigtastene: CTRL + SHIFT + Delete. Hvis hurtigtastene ikke virker, eller hvis du bruker MAC, finn ut hvilken nettleser du bruker og klikk på relevant link: Internet Explorer Mozilla Firefox Google Chrome Opera Safari Flash cookies Apple Android Windows 7 Husk: Hvis du bruker flere nettlesere, må du slette cookies i alle. Har du spørsmål? Hvis du har kommentarer eller spørsmål i forbindelse med informasjon og/eller behandling av personlige opplysninger, er du velkommen til å ta kontakt med oss. Cookiedeklarasjonen oppdateres hver måned av Cookie Information . Hvis du har spørsmål til den, kan du skrive til info@cookieinformation.com. Kategori for samtykke Godkjenn alle Funksjonelle Statistiske Markedsføring Gå til innhold Gå til sidemeny Jobbnorge.no needs JavaScript for all functions to work properly. Please turn on JavaScript in your browser and try again. 15th November 2026 Languages English English English Research assistants in VaccAI and CuratedAI at MediaFutures Apply for this job See advertisement UiB Knowledge that shapes society UiB shall be among Europe’s leading universities, internationally recognized for high quality in research and education. As a societal institution, we shall contribute to sustainable and democratic development and be an attractive and inclusive place to study and work. ... (Video unable to load from YouTube. Accept cookie and refresh page to watch video, or click here to open video) Research assistants There are two research assistant vacancies linked to VaccAI and CuratedAI at the Department of Information Science and Media Studies, University of Bergen, in the MediaFutures research environment. The positions will support research led by Professor Christoph Trattner. VaccAI: one 40% position starting as soon as possible after the application deadline of 15 November 2026, by agreement, and ending on 30 September 2028. CuratedAI: one 30% position starting as soon as possible after the application deadline of 15 November 2026, by agreement, and ending on 30 September 2028. Research assistant is a recruitment position supporting academic staff in their teaching and research. The positions provide an opportunity to gain insight into scientific work and methodology. Total employment as a research assistant cannot exceed two years. About the projects VaccAI is a Research Council of Norway funded project examining vaccine related claims in the news and the information environment surrounding vaccination. The project combines analysis of news content with research on how people encounter and evaluate health information. Research assistants will help prepare and analyse research material and support empirical studies of vaccine communication and AI assisted approaches to assessing claims. CuratedAI is a Research Council of Norway funded project examining artificial intelligence and transparency in journalism. It investigates how the use of AI in producing and verifying news can be communicated to audiences, and how transparency measures affect their understanding and evaluation of news. The research includes AI disclosure, provenance and watermarking approaches, and the needs of journalists and the public. About MediaFutures MediaFutures is a Centre for Research based Innovation hosted by the Department of Information Science and Media Studies at the University of Bergen, with its primary workplace at Media City Bergen. In collaboration with news media and technology partners, the centre develops responsible media technology and investigates media experiences, recommender systems, content production and analysis, and audience interaction. Read more at www.mediafutures.no . Work tasks The research assistants will formally report to the PI of the two projects Professor Christoph Trattner and support the relevant project teams in scientific, technical and project related administrative tasks. Tasks may include: Preparing, collecting, cleaning and documenting research data, including news content, survey responses and experimental data. Programming research tools, setting up study infrastructure and supporting online surveys and experiments. Reviewing literature, annotating research material and assisting with quantitative or qualitative analyses. Contributing to research documentation, reports, publications and dissemination activities. Providing practical and administrative support directly related to the assigned project. In VaccAI, the work will focus on vaccine related news and health claims. In CuratedAI, it will focus on AI use in journalism, transparency and audience responses. Specific tasks will be agreed according to project needs and the successful candidates’ qualifications. Qualifications and personal qualities Applicants should, as a minimum, be bachelor’s students in information science, media studies, computer science or another relevant discipline. ICT competence and programming skills are required. Proficiency in written and spoken English and Norwegian is required. Applicants should be structured, solution oriented and able to work both independently and collaboratively. Experience with data collection, data analysis, surveys or experiments is an advantage. An interest in health communication and vaccine information is relevant to VaccAI; an interest in journalism, AI transparency and audience research is relevant to CuratedAI. Knowledge of the MediaFutures research environment and the media or technology sector is an advantage. We can offer A good and professionally challenging working environment, with opportunities to gain practical research experience. Salary according to the applicable research assistant category: Gross annual salary as research assistant for bachelor students (code 1018) NOK 455 000, -. For candidates with a bachelor’s degree (code 1019), the gross annual salary will be NOK 470 200.-. For candidates with a master’s degree (code 1020), the annual salary will be NOK 519 400,-. The salary mentioned is for a 100% position. Enrolment in the Norwegian Public Service Pension Fund and good welfare benefits. Primary workplace at Media City Bergen. Your application must include An application letter describing your motivation and relevant experience. Please indicate whether you are applying for VaccAI, CuratedAI or both positions. A CV, copies of diplomas, certificates of education and other relevant documents, with certified translations into English or a Scandinavian language where required. Applications and attachments must be uploaded through Jobbnorge using the “Apply for this job” link. Application deadline: 15 November 2026. Potential candidates will be invited for an interview. Generell informasjon: For further information about the positions, please contact PI Professor Christoph Trattner at christoph.trattner@uib.no. Practical questions about the application process should be directed to HR at personal.svfa@uib.no . Diversity is a strength that enables us to solve our tasks even better. UiB therefore needs qualified employees regardless of gender, ethnicity, religion, worldview, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression and age. The University of Bergen applies the principle of public access to information when recruiting staff for academic positions. Information about applicants may be made public even if an applicant has asked not to be named on the list of applicants. Applicants will be notified if their request to be omitted is not granted. We encourage applicants with disabilities, immigrant backgrounds or gaps in their CV to apply. By indicating such circumstances in your application, you may receive favourable consideration. At least one qualified applicant from each of these groups will be invited for an interview as part of our commitment to inclusivity and equal opportunity. via Unsplash via Unsplash About UiB The University of Bergen is a renowned educational and research institution, organised into seven faculties and approximately 54 institutes and academic centres. Campus is located in the centre of Bergen with university areas at Nygårdshøyden, Haukeland, Marineholmen, Møllendalsveien and Årstad. There are seven departments at Faculty of Social Sciences. Read more about the faculty and departments . Apply for this job Deadline 15th November 2026 Employer University of Bergen Municipality Bergen Scope Part time (2 positions) Part time (%) Duration Fixed Term Place of service postboks 7802, 5020  Bergen Loading... See more jobs Vacant positions -   University of Bergen Back to search PDF Link to startpage Switchboard: +47 75 54 22 20 Support Privacy policy - cookies"
    },
